Reach a server through a proxy.

On a network that cuts the connection to a Mumble server, or blocks it, you can now dial through an HTTP or SOCKS5 proxy — for one server or for all of them, with voice going straight to the server or through the proxy too. A proxy can be shared by link or QR code, like a server.

Also: links in welcome messages and channel descriptions work, a channel you may not speak in is marked, and groups and permissions can be managed in the app.
